{ "Identifier":       { "ImplementerID": "1", "ImplementationID": "OSD-3OD-V1.5-I01", "AIMName": "OSD-3OD-V1.5" },
  "APIProfile":       "Basic",
  "Description":      "3D Model Object Delivery: delivers a 3D scene to a device - a 3D renderer - keeping each object typed to the device edge, where the device renders it (3D to 2D on the screen). It delivers the 3D Model (Basic 3D Model Object or 3D Model Object) together with the animation streams that drive it - Face Descriptors (facial animation) and Body Descriptors (body animation) - each on its own port, so further animation streams can be added independently. The model and its animation are inseparable at render time (posing is rendering). Independent of the other Object Delivery AIMs.",
